# Force LF in the working tree for authored Lua. Without this a fresh clone on a machine
# with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF for every .lua, and the two locale tools then disagree:
# ../EverythingLocales/scan.py writes the manifest with a fixed LF, while build.py keeps
# whatever ending the file already had - so the four Locales files end up mixed. Git hides
# it either way, because autocrlf normalizes on the way into the index.
*.lua text eol=lf
